# (LADDER-ARMS i1) the lying sword: flat on the ground along the corpse's lower edge, the grip by the near hand and the
# blade toward the feet (never standing up: the owner, 2026-10-23). Screen-space at the body's pivot (mirrored head east).
# (polish i1 integration) 6 px further toward the feet: the legs now lie with the body and hid the blade.
# (LADDER-ARMS i2) laid after the turn (`anchor pivot`) along the legs' lower edge, the blade past the boots, so the
# lying kite no longer hides it; every swing, guard and drop view now marks its finish regions (R guard and pommel, G the
# pommel, P the flat, N a 3 px rune dash by the guard; the drawn guard / gmove views R only: C13's glow budget)
view L key drop origin -8 -2 anchor pivot layer heldBack
